# VALRUNE

An Android 2D top-down space shooter. Godot 4.7.1 / GDScript. Solo developer working
through an AI assistant, so the repository is the memory and the documents are the contract.

## Reading order and authority

**`docs/decisions/0000-decision-log.md` is authoritative.** The numbered documents in
`docs/` are **v0** — written before the ability and status spreadsheets were reconciled.
Several of their decisions have been reversed. Where a v0 document conflicts with the
decision log, **the decision log wins.** Every v0 file carries a banner saying so.

| Path | Contains |
|---|---|
| `docs/decisions/` | Decision log + ADRs. **Authoritative.** |
| `docs/00`–`13` | v0 design documents. Revised in Phase 7. |
| `docs/14-CANON.md` | Glossary. Every term and its code identifier. *(Phase 1a)* |
| `docs/15-CONSTANTS.md` | Geometry bands, playfield units, naming. *(Phase 1b)* |
| `docs/16-STATUS-EFFECTS.md` | Status catalog, tags, immunity/override. *(Phase 1d)* |
| `docs/17-BALANCE-METHOD.md` | Power metrics and profiles. *(Phase 4)* |
| `data/source/` | The original spreadsheet brain dump. Input, not schema. |
| `data/` | Generated, validated JSON. Source of truth for balance. |

## Current phase

The project is in **planning**, not implementation. `game/` is empty and stays empty
until the M0 control prototype. Do not scaffold Godot code, write GDScript, or create
scenes unless the task explicitly says M0 has started.

## Before implementing anything

Read the relevant document first. If a request conflicts with `docs/decisions/`, say so
and ask — do not silently deviate. If a decision is genuinely new, write it into the
decision log as part of the work.

## Vocabulary

Terms are defined in `docs/14-CANON.md` and are not interchangeable. In particular
**gun** (a mount), **gun-shot** (one trigger event across all mounts), and **projectile**
(one bullet from one mount) mean different things, as do **basic attack** and **ability**
on the baddie side. Use the defined term.

Elements are PLASMA, CRYO, FORGE, VOLT, CAUSTIC (base) and CHRONO, GAMMA, VOID, ETHER
(DLC). It is **ETHER**, never AETHER.
